            <div xml:id="d615">

                <pb facs="0669" n="657" sameAs="frus:frus1942v05/pg657"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.3332/128: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-04-10T20:00:00-04:00">April 10, 1942—8 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>931. In view of the reported presence of enemy submarines off the Brazilian
                    coast, the Navy Department urgently requests blanket permission to operate
                    United States Navy patrol planes from the land fields at Fortaleza and São Luiz
                    without prior notification. Notification by the local United States naval
                    commanding officer at Natal to the local authorities would of course be made at
                    the time of beginning the operations. The area of particular interest is roughly
                    that stretch of the coast between São Luiz and Fortaleza.</p>
                <p>This request does not involve the use of additional planes but only the amphibian
                    planes operating from Natal at present.</p>
                <p>You may use your discretion in approaching Brazilian authorities. Urgent reply
                    requested.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
